     "items": [
      {
       "q": "How does the app cost calculator work?",
       "a": "It estimates the weeks of senior engineering your app needs from the stage, features, backend, platforms and design you choose, then multiplies by an indicative weekly rate. Our guide to <a href=\"/blog/app-cost-estimator\">how an app cost estimator works</a> explains the method."
      },
      {
       "q": "How accurate is the estimate?",
       "a": "It is an indicative planning range, not a quote. Your exact fixed price is confirmed after a short discovery call once requirements are clear."
      },
      {
       "q": "How much does it cost to build a mobile app?",
       "a": "It depends on scope. In our model a lean MVP is about 7 weeks and a market-ready product about 25 weeks. See <a href=\"/blog/mobile-app-cost-examples\">three worked examples with real numbers</a>."
      },
      {
       "q": "Is it cheaper to build only for iOS or only for Android?",
       "a": "Slightly. A single platform is about 10 percent less than building both from one shared codebase, because most of the work is shared. See <a href=\"/blog/android-app-development-cost\">Android app development cost</a>."
      },
      {
       "q": "Which features add the most to the cost?",
       "a": "Payments, chat, maps, offline sync, AI integration and an admin dashboard each add real weeks. Accounts and push notifications are comparatively cheap."
      },
      {
       "q": "Is the calculator free, and do I need to sign up?",
       "a": "It is free and the estimate appears instantly. You only enter an email if you want the detailed breakdown sent to you."
      }
     ]
    }
